  ...SPEAK('K4', 'Speaking, A brand I follow online',
    'Talk for about 1 minute about a brand or shop you follow on social media.\n• Which brand is it, and on which platform do you follow it?\n• What kind of content does it post?\n• Have you ever bought something because of its posts or livestreams? Why or why not?',
    'I follow a small clothes shop called Nha May on TikTok. It has about fifty thousand followers. The shop posts short videos every day. They show new T-shirts and give ideas about what to wear to university. It also runs a livestream every Sunday evening. I have bought two T-shirts from the livestream because there was a discount and free delivery. I like the content because it is funny and useful, so I have shared some videos with my friends.',
    'Content: names the brand and platform, describes its content, and says whether the speaker has bought anything and why'),
  ...WRITE('K4', 'Writing, A short results report',
    'You help Ms Hoa, the owner of an online flower shop, with social media. Write a short report of about 100 words for her. Purpose: summarise this month\'s results and suggest one action.\nData — TikTok: followers 5,000 → 6,500; video views 80,000; orders 30. Facebook: followers 3,000 → 3,100; orders 55.\n• Describe the results on TikTok.\n• Describe the results on Facebook.\n• Make one suggestion for next month.',
    'To: Ms Hoa\nSubject: Social media results for this month\n\nThis month has been good for the shop.\n\nOn TikTok, our followers have increased from 5,000 to 6,500, and our videos have reached 80,000 views. However, TikTok has brought only 30 orders.\n\nOn Facebook, growth has been slow. We have gained only 100 new followers. But Facebook has brought 55 orders, so our customers there buy more often.\n\nFor next month, I suggest that we add a link to the shop in every TikTok video. This will make it easier for viewers to order. We should also continue posting on Facebook three times a week.',
    'Content: describes the TikTok and Facebook results accurately from the data and makes one clear suggestion'),

